# 5. The general engine promises next-open execution but doesn't have open prices

`BacktestEngine` documents:

> signal at bar t → execute at bar t+1 open.

But it pivots only `close`, calculates close-to-close returns, shifts positions one row and applies those returns.

That creates an execution semantic ambiguity.

If a position supposedly begins at `open(t+1)` but its PnL includes the move from `close(t)` to `close(t+1)`, it captures the overnight/opening gap it did not own.

### Required resolution

There must be one explicitly defined fill convention.

Example:

```text
decision at t close
fill at t+1 open
holding return =
    exit_price / actual_fill_price - 1
```

Do not derive trading PnL by shifting a weight series unless the return interval exactly matches the ownership interval.

For correctness, I prefer an event ledger first, then vectorize later after equivalence tests.

