# 6. Missing observations are converted into economic zeroes

This is particularly dangerous for dying/illiquid tokens.

Production backtesting uses patterns such as:

```text
pct_change().fill_null(0)
funding_rate.fill_null(0)
```

That implies:

> "we have no reliable price observation"

becomes:

> "the asset returned exactly 0%."

And:

> "we lack funding"

becomes:

> "funding was exactly zero."

Those are completely different statements.

The repo has an invariant asserting missing returns must not become zero, but that invariant tests `compute_log_returns()`, not the production backtesting path that performs the zero-fill.

Even metrics later use `nan_to_num(..., nan=0)`, which can hide corruption in an equity curve.

## Correct rule: fail closed

Missingness must produce one of:

```text
MISSING_PRICE
STALE_PRICE
NO_FUNDING_OBSERVATION
NOT_TRADABLE
INSUFFICIENT_HISTORY
```

Then either:

* abstain from opening;
* explicitly carry an already-open position using an approved mark policy;
* or invalidate the backtest if settlement cannot be established.

Never silently invent 0.

