# 7. Funding accounting is not currently trustworthy

There are several separate problems.

## 7.1 One funding rate is applied to aggregate short gross

The main engine expects a funding frame essentially keyed only by timestamp and applies:

```text
funding_rate × total short gross
```

rather than individual funding per asset.

But:

```text
BTC funding != W funding != PHA funding
```

Each open position requires its own settlement event.

## 7.2 Funding is carried forward and can be charged repeatedly

`compute_funding_pnl_series()` takes the most recent funding observation at or before each backtest observation and applies it again.

If the funding payment occurs every eight hours but you're processing hourly rows, that can count the same settlement multiple times.

Funding must be an **event**, not a state continuously multiplied at each arbitrary bar.

## 7.3 Annualization semantics disagree

`features/funding.py` says rates are per eight-hour period, but annualizes with:

```text
rate × 24 × 365
```

which corresponds to hourly funding.

Period duration must be part of the source schema.

### Required representation

```text
FundingEvent {
    venue
    instrument_id
    settlement_time
    rate
    period_hours
    known_at
}
```

For every open position:

```text
funding_pnl =
    signed_notional_at_settlement
    × funding_rate
```

exactly once per settlement.

