# 8. The main backtest ranking selects all candidate shorts

In `_simulate_split()`:

```text
n_shorts = len(short_symbols)
top_n = min(n_shorts, number_valid)
```

Therefore every valid `short_symbol` receives the maximum short weight.

The cross-sectional ranking barely matters.

For five assets and:

```text
max_short_weight = 0.35
```

this can imply:

```text
short gross = 1.75
```

despite config saying:

```text
max_short_gross = 1.25
```

The general simulator does not enforce many of the declared portfolio constraints.

The separate optimizer also declares constraints such as min/max short gross, net exposure and max turnover, but not all are actually supplied to SLSQP.

## Correct rule

Every bar after target generation and after fill must satisfy:

```text
abs(weight_i) <= max_name_weight

min_short_gross <= short_gross <= max_short_gross

min_net <= net_exposure <= max_net

turnover <= max_turnover

position_notional <= ADV participation limit
```

Violation:

```text
raise PortfolioInvariantViolation
```

Never log-and-continue.

