# 11. `validate_tokens()` is not validation

The routine identifies tokens that eventually suffered large realized drawdowns, then goes backward and asks whether they had high death scores beforehand.

That is an interesting case study but statistically it is:

```text
select assets based on future bad outcome
→ inspect historical score
```

It has no proper false-positive denominator.

Suppose the model also flagged 300 tokens that subsequently moonshot. The current retrospective test would not tell us.

### Replace with prospective classification

For every eligible `(asset, date)` establish the label **without conditioning the sample on the result**:

```text
Y_30d_short_profit
Y_30d_underperform_btc
Y_30d_underperform_market
Y_30d_drawdown
Y_stopout_before_target
```

Evaluate all candidates.

Then calculate:

```text
precision
recall
ROC-AUC
PR-AUC
Brier score
log loss
top-decile lift
expected return by score decile
calibration
```

