# 12. Survivorship / point-in-time universe is not enforced

The death script loops over whichever Binance JSON files exist in the repository today.

That is not a historical universe.

The generic `markets` table is also essentially one current/static row per symbol rather than a versioned listing lifecycle.

And although `BacktestEngine` exposes a `universe` parameter, it explicitly doesn't use it.

The paper trader additionally uses a hand-maintained present-day `BLUE_CHIPS` exclusion list.

That is especially dangerous. A token's future survival/quality can leak backward through membership in that list.

## Required universe schema

```text
UniverseMembership {
    venue
    instrument_id
    tradable_from
    tradable_to
    announcement_known_at
    perpetual_available_from
    perpetual_available_to
    shortable
    max_leverage
    status
}
```

At time `t`, candidate selection must be:

```text
tradable_from <= t < tradable_to
AND known_at <= t
AND sufficient_history == true
AND liquidity constraints satisfied
```

Delisted and failed coins must remain in the historical dataset.

