# 13. The data store cannot currently reconstruct "what was known then"

BEAR needs **bitemporal data**.

Today the store commonly:

```text
DELETE historical rows for symbol
INSERT refreshed history
```

which throws away previous revisions/backfills.

A backtest of fundamentals/tokenomics needs to distinguish:

```text
effective_at:
when the thing was economically true

known_at:
when the market could first know it

ingested_at:
when BEAR obtained it
```

Those are not interchangeable.

Example:

```text
Unlock occurs:       Dec 1
Unlock announced:    Oct 1
BEAR captured it:    Oct 2
Schedule revised:    Nov 10
```

At Oct 15 the model may know the original Dec 1 unlock.

It must **not** know the Nov 10 revision.

## Required immutable event schema

Every research datum should have:

```text
source
venue
instrument_id
effective_at
known_at
ingested_at
revision_id
payload_hash
source_version
```

Never overwrite.

Backtest reads:

```text
WHERE known_at <= decision_time
```

and chooses the latest revision that was known by then.

