# 15. Some feature modules use today's knowledge inside historical calculations

This is another serious class of lookahead.

`compute_unlock_pressure()` calls:

```python
datetime.now(timezone.utc)
```

internally.

Therefore it is inherently a "current snapshot" function, not a historical point-in-time feature.

`compute_listing_features()` also uses the present time and latest prices. Cohort return calculation can consume the eventual full first-to-last return of other cohort assets.

That can inject future information directly into historical features.

## Rule

Nothing in:

```text
features/
labels/
backtest/
model/
```

may call `datetime.now()`.

Every function receives:

```text
as_of: UTC timestamp
```

explicitly.

Add a static CI test that AST-scans these packages and fails if `datetime.now`, `date.today`, etc. appear.

