# 17. The current IC evaluator is not calculating proper cross-sectional IC

For a cross-sectional crypto signal the information coefficient at time `t` should normally be:

```text
Spearman(
    factor values across assets at t,
    future returns across those same assets
)
```

This gives:

```text
IC_t
```

Then statistical analysis operates on:

```text
IC_1, IC_2, ..., IC_T
```

Instead the evaluator extracts factor and forward-return columns by row position and computes correlations across flattened/rolling rows. It doesn't even require a join on `(timestamp, symbol)`.

That makes results sensitive to row ordering and mixes time-series and cross-sectional variation.

## Required implementation

```text
for each timestamp t:
    universe = eligible assets at t
    x = feature(asset,t)
    y = forward_return(asset,t,h)
    IC[t] = Spearman(x,y)
```

Then:

```text
mean_IC
ICIR
HAC t-stat
fraction_IC_positive
IC by regime
```

Use FDR correction when testing many factors.

### Binary test

Shuffle the ordering of all panel rows.

Every timestamp IC and final statistic must remain exactly unchanged.

