# 18. Lasso preprocessing currently leaks validation data

`lasso_select()` does:

```python
scaler.fit_transform(X)
TimeSeriesSplit(...)
LassoCV(...)
```

So the scaler observes the entire dataset before cross-validation.

Additionally, flattened panel rows can cause a normal row-based `TimeSeriesSplit` to put assets from the same timestamp on opposite sides of a fold boundary.

### Required architecture

Use date-block folds.

All assets belonging to timestamp `t` belong to exactly one fold.

All preprocessing belongs inside the fitted pipeline:

```text
Pipeline(
    imputer,
    scaler,
    model
)
```

and `.fit()` receives training data only.

If using standard time-series split tooling, remember that `gap` can exclude observations adjacent to a test period, but with overlapping financial labels we should purge by the actual label interval, not merely a fixed arbitrary row count. ([scikit-learn][4])

