# 23. Separate four different kinds of uncertainty

Do not collapse all uncertainty into one number.

## A. Prediction probability

```text
P(trade profitable | current features)
```

from calibrated OOS predictions.

## B. Outcome uncertainty

```text
q10/q50/q90 future return
```

from quantile/distributional modelling.

## C. Statistical uncertainty around the model

For example:

```text
OOS Sharpe:
0.83
95% block-bootstrap CI: [0.19, 1.39]
```

## D. Data quality / OOD

```text
data_completeness = 0.94
OOD = false
```

These are conceptually different.

---

# 24. Confidence intervals must respect time dependence

Do not bootstrap individual token rows randomly.

Crypto assets move together.

A portfolio with 15 names on one date does not create 15 independent macro observations.

Bootstrap by:

```text
rebalance date blocks
weeks/months
market regimes
```

Use block bootstrap for confidence intervals around:

```text
mean return
Sharpe
hit rate
drawdown
IC
calibration metrics
```

For sequential prediction intervals, standard conformal inference's exchangeability assumptions are problematic; adaptive/time-series conformal approaches are better suited to changing dependent sequences. ([Proceedings of Machine Learning Research][6])

