# 39. Multiple testing protection

Implement three complementary methods.

### Deflated Sharpe Ratio

Use to ask:

> Given non-normal returns and all the strategy variants we tried, how impressive is this Sharpe really?

([DOI.org][1])

### PBO / CSCV

Use to ask:

> When we pick the best-looking strategy in one partition, how frequently is it poor out of sample?

([eScholarship][2])

### SPA / Reality Check

Use when comparing a large family of strategies against a benchmark while accounting for data snooping. ([Taylor & Francis Online][3])

Store every attempted strategy so these calculations have a credible trial universe.

