# 41. Individual trade gating

The strategy does not need to trade every prediction.

A candidate can expose:

```text
P_profit = 0.67
E_return = +3.2%
q10 = -8.4%
estimated_cost = 0.7%
P_stopout = 0.12
OOD = false
data_completeness = 0.94
```

Then deterministic policy:

```text
trade iff:

P_profit >= calibrated_threshold
AND E_return - estimated_cost >= required_edge
AND P_stopout <= max_allowed
AND OOD == false
AND data_completeness >= threshold
AND liquidity constraints pass
```

The model estimates probability.

The policy decides whether that probability offers adequate risk-adjusted economics.

