# Final instruction

**Do not attempt to salvage the existing Sharpe by incrementally patching `backtest_death.py`.**

Build the correctness layer first, make the current system fail the P0 tests, repair it until every gate passes, and then rerun the strategy completely from scratch.

The first number I want to see after the rebuild is not Sharpe.

I want:

```text
VERIFICATION: 24 / 24 HARD GATES PASS
DATA SNAPSHOT: <hash>
MODEL: <hash>
OUTER OOS PREDICTIONS: <n>
INDEPENDENT TEST BLOCKS: <n>
```

Only after that should BEAR print the Sharpe.

The single most important engineering principle here is **future-mutation invariance**: changing anything after decision time must be mathematically incapable of changing that decision. Combined with immutable `known_at` data, timestamp-keyed panels, exact train/serve parity, and a fill ledger, it catches most of the subtle leakage classes that currently affect BEAR.

